{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "process-refueling fixture",
    "description": "The `process-refueling` fixture: 336 rows of MOVESOutput -- Total Gaseous Hydrocarbons from Refueling Displacement Vapor Loss (process 18) and Refueling Spillage Loss (process 19) for passenger cars on urban restricted-access roads in Washtenaw County, August, 7am, 2020 -- computed from the snapshot's own INPUT tables. It ports docs/process-refueling.md end to end.\n\nWHAT IS STRUCTURALLY NEW. `RefuelingLossCalculator` is the first calculator in this port that does not compute a rate on the running-exhaust spine at all. It is CHAINED: it subscribes to no MasterLoop stage, hangs off `BaseRateCalculator`, and reads that calculator's Total Energy Consumption output as its ACTIVITY (`calculator-dag.json`: subscribes_directly false, depends_on BaseRateCalculator). Its whole arithmetic is\n\n    emissionQuant = lossRate x energy / (energyContent x fuelDensity)\n\n-- energy divided by kJ-per-gallon is GALLONS delivered, and both loss rates are grams of THC per gallon. So the fixture reuses docs/mixed-onroad.md's spine unchanged -- the activity chain S1-S9, the cohort structure and fuel-usage rebase S10-S12, the drive-cycle operating-mode weights `dc_W`, the base rate S13-S14 and the calculator's adjustments S15 -- and everything downstream of it is new.\n\nTHE ENERGY IS IN KILOJOULES AND MUST NOT BE REBASED. S18's kilojoule-to-MillionBTU divisor is applied by the output processor AFTER every chained calculator has run (moves-framework engine.rs:1078-1086), so `rtDay_energyQuant` is deliberately undivided; the divisor is applied to the EMITTED row instead, where both refueling pollutant-processes compute it to be exactly 1 because Total Gaseous Hydrocarbons is a mass pollutant.\n\nTHE ENERGY SPINE IS A SELF-JOIN, not a second relation. The run carries seven pollutant-processes: two refueling (118, 119), two Total Organic Gases on the same processes (8618, 8619) which a downstream speciation calculator produces, and three Total Energy Consumption (9101 running, 9102 start, 9190 extended idle) which the refueling formulae consume. All seven ride one flat `rate_rows = 7 x 164` relation, and the refueling row reads its cohort's energy back through a `syms`-named self-join of that relation -- the same shape process-brakewear's PM10 chain uses. Two of the three energy pollutant-processes contribute EXACTLY ZERO, and the fixture measures that rather than assuming it: start rates live on operating modes 101-108 and extended-idle rates on mode 200, `dc_W` covers the 23 running modes of an on-network road type, and `run_offNetworkRoadTypeCount` is 0.\n\nTWO BLOCKS OF DIFFERENT SIZES, which is why there is one rank and not a per-block cohort ordinal. 336 = 64 displacement cohorts + 104 spillage cohorts, times 2 day types. `refuelingcontroltechnology` carries fuel types 1 and 5 only, so displacement loses the 40 diesel cohorts spillage keeps; and REFEC-7's inner join onto RefuelingFuelType drops all 21 electricity cohorts from both, because `fuelsubtype.energyContent` and `fueltype.fuelDensity` are NULL for electricity. `rt_refuelRank` numbers the survivors 1..168 by an inclusive prefix count over the whole rate relation (docs/esm-conventions.md 22).\n\nCOMPUTED, from the input tables and nothing else: every number. NO REFERENCE TABLE IS AN INPUT. `baserate_1_2020`, `baserate_2_2020`, `baserate_90_2020`, `baserateoutput`, `sourcebindistribution`, `sho` and `MOVESOutput` are all generator or expected output, and none of them is a `data_sources` entry here. Values out of the first and the last DO appear as `expected` in the inline tests below, which is the opposite direction.\n\nDECLARED: one number, `n_outputRefuelRow` = 168. WHICH 168 of the 1,148 candidate rate rows survive is a result of the chain and is never written down; `run_refuelRowCount` recomputes 168 and `pp_refuelRowCount` recomputes the 64 and the 104 separately.\n\nWHAT THIS FIXTURE CANNOT SEE, stated because docs/esm-conventions.md 23 requires it: both Stage II program reductions are exactly 0 in this county and year, so the two (1 - P) factors are 1 and perturbing either moves no output cell. components/refueling_loss_rate.esm carries them at 0.2 and 0.3, along with both arms of the refueling-temperature clamp, both arms of the tank-temperature-difference clamp and both readings of the minimum-vapour-loss sentinel -- none of which this fixture's own temperature reaches.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "moves",
      "onroad",
      "refueling",
      "evaporative",
      "fixture",
      "process-refueling"
    ]
  },
