          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The A term actually used: the exact-class row if there is one, the regClassID 0 wildcard otherwise, and zero if neither. Only the energy pollutant-processes have a row of either kind, so the four others get a temperature factor of exactly 1 from the standard quadratic with zero terms."
        },
        "rt_tempAdjustTermB": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The B term actually used: the exact-class row if there is one, the regClassID 0 wildcard otherwise, and zero if neither. Only the energy pollutant-processes have a row of either kind, so the four others get a temperature factor of exactly 1 from the standard quadratic with zero terms."
        },
