            "from": {
              "file_variable": "fuelDensity"
            }
          }
        },
        "run_offNetworkRoadTypeID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "run_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The off-network road type, 1 -- the road type BaseRateGenerator puts START and HOTELLING rates on. Carried as a one-row relation so the count below is a `join.on` and not an `==` inside a filter (docs/esm-conventions.md 20.4)."
        },
        "run_offNetworkRoadTypeCount": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "run_rows"
          ],
          "description": "How many of the RunSpec's road types are the off-network one. ZERO, and the whole energy spine below depends on it: processes 2, 90 and 91 emit their rates off-network, so with no off-network road type selected their operating modes (101-108 for starts, 200 for extended idle) never appear in `dc_W` and their contribution to the chained energy is exactly 0. `pp_energyTotal` measures that zero; this counts the reason for it, and a retarget onto a RunSpec that DID select road type 1 would make this 1 and the argument invalid."
        },
        "run_refuelingVaporProgramAdjust": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "run_rows"
          ],
          "description": "countyyear.refuelingVaporProgramAdjust for the run's county and year: the Stage II vapour-recovery reduction P. Exactly 0 in Washtenaw County in 2020."
        },
        "run_refuelingSpillProgramAdjust": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "run_rows"
          ],
          "description": "countyyear.refuelingSpillProgramAdjust: the Stage II spillage reduction. Also exactly 0."
        },
        "rspp_isEnergySource": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "runspecpollutantprocess_rows"
          ],
          "description": "Whether this pollutant-process is one of the Total Energy Consumption records the refueling formulae CONSUME: pollutant 91 crossed with running (1), start (2), extended-idle (90) and auxiliary-power (91) exhaust. That set is refueling_loss_calculator.rs's own ENERGY_SOURCE_PROCESS_IDS, the SQL's `mwo.processID IN (1, 2, 90, 91)`. Three of the run's seven qualify -- 9101, 9102 and 9190 -- and only the first contributes anything, for the road-type reason `run_offNetworkRoadTypeCount` records."
        },
        "rspp_refuelingProcessID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "runspecpollutantprocess_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The refueling process this pollutant-process PRODUCES, and 0 -- no process -- for one that does not. RefuelingLossCalculator's Java `pollutantIDs` array is {1}, and `subscribeToMe` INTERSECTS the RunSpec's (pollutant, process) selections with it (refueling_loss_calculator.rs:2505-2521). That intersection is what this column is: the run also selects 8618 and 8619, Total Organic Gases on the same two processes, and those are produced downstream by TOG speciation chaining off THIS calculator's output, not by it. Keying on the process alone would give them a refueling rate and 168 spurious rows."
        },
        "ffm_RVPValue": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "fuelformulation_rows"
          ],
          "description": "fuelformulation.RVP with the NULL treated as no contribution. `RVP` is nullable and a NULL arrives from the parquet reader as NaN; `sum(RVP x marketShare)` over a NaN is NaN, and multiplying by a 0/1 presence indicator does not fix it because 0 x NaN is NaN. `ifelse` selects its branch before evaluating it, which is what makes this the fix."
        },
        "fst_energyContentValue": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "fuelsubtype_rows"
          ],
          "description": "fuelsubtype.energyContent under the RefuelingFuelType extract's own `WHERE energyContent > 0`, written as a value for the same NaN reason: electricity's is NULL."
        },
        "ftp_fuelDensityValue": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "fueltype_rows"
          ],
          "description": "fueltype.fuelDensity under `WHERE fuelDensity > 0`. Electricity's is NULL."
        },
        "fsp_isInRunSupply": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "fuelsupply_rows"
          ],
          "description": "Whether this fuel-supply row is the run county's, through `regioncounty`. A SEMI-JOIN and not a value lookup: `regioncounty` carries TWO rows for this county, one per regionCodeID, so summing the region id over them would give 540000000 and matching nothing (docs/esm-conventions.md 3)."
        },
        "fsp_isInRunMonth": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "fuelsupply_rows"
          ],
          "description": "Whether the supply row's month GROUP contains the run's month. REFEC-2 fans each monthGroup-keyed supply row across every month of its group and then reads the run month's cell back; with one month in scope that is this presence test."
        },
        "fsp_isSelected": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "fuelsupply_rows"
          ],
          "description": "Both scope gates. All five rows pass here -- the extract is already the run's -- and the gates are written because a snapshot with more than one region or month group would need them and would fail silently without them."
        },
        "fsp_fuelSubtypeID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "fuelsupply_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The formulation's fuel subtype."
        },
        "fsp_RVP": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "fuelsupply_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The formulation's Reid vapour pressure."
        },
        "fsp_fuelTypeID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "fuelsupply_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The formulation's fuel TYPE, through its subtype. 0 -- the additive identity, and no fuel type -- for formulation 28001, whose subtype 30 is absent from `fuelsubtype` altogether; that is an INNER JOIN miss in the reference and it has to stay one here."
        },
        "fsp_energyContent": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "fuelsupply_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The subtype's energy content, kJ per gram."
        },
        "rff_averageRVP": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "refuelingfactors_rows"
          ],
          "description": "REFEC-2: sum(RVP x marketShare) over the run's fuel supply, by fuel type. 8.0 for gasoline, 7.7 for E85, 0 for diesel and electricity -- and the 0 for diesel is a REAL sum over a formulation whose RVP is 0, not a missing row."
        },
        "rff_energyContent": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "refuelingfactors_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The RefuelingFuelType extract: sum(marketShare x energyContent) by (fuel type, month). 41.696 gasoline, 42.7 diesel, 29.12 E85, and 0 for electricity because its subtype's energyContent is NULL."
        },
        "rff_fuelDensity": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
