          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "refuelingfactors_rows"
          ],
          "description": "kJ per gallon. Dividing the chained Total Energy Consumption by it converts energy to fuel VOLUME, which is what both refueling rates are per."
        },
        "rff_hasFuelDivisor": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "refuelingfactors_rows"
          ],
          "description": "REFEC-7's INNER JOIN onto RefuelingFuelType, whose extract keeps only `energyContent > 0 AND fuelDensity > 0`. Electricity fails BOTH, so every electricity energy row is dropped before either refueling rate is applied -- which is why the spillage block is 104 cohorts and not 125, even though `sourcetypetechadjustment` gives electricity a spillage rate."
        },
        "rff_temperature": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
