          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The run's Stage II spillage reduction BEFORE the fuel-type fan-out below decides whether this fuel keeps it."
        },
        "spcy_fuelTypeID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "spillage_county_year_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The five fuel types `RefuelingLossCalculator.sql`'s spillage section synthesises onto RefuelingCountyYear. The SQL ALTERs a fuelTypeID column in (existing rows default to gasoline), duplicates the gasoline row as E85 -- most Stage II programs cover E85 too -- and INSERTs zero-adjustment rows for 2, 3 and 9. That is model logic that happens to be written as DDL, so it is ported as a relation and not as a branch (refueling_loss_calculator.rs:221-222, SPILLAGE_COUNTY_YEAR_FUEL_TYPES)."
        },
        "spcy_retainsProgramAdjust": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "spillage_county_year_rows"
          ],
          "description": "Whether the synthesised row keeps the county's refuelingSpillProgramAdjust or zeroes it. Gasoline and E85 keep it; 2, 3 and 9 are inserted with zero. It is inert in THIS run -- the county's adjustment is 0, so both arms give 0 -- and it is written because the two arms differ the moment a Stage II county is run."
        },
        "rt_hasSpillCountyYear": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows"
          ],
          "description": "Whether the fan-out synthesised a county-year row for this fuel type. All four of the run's fuels are in the five, so this is 1 everywhere here; it is the second half of the spillage existence test and the half a CNG run would need."
        },
        "rt_spillProgramAdjust": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The spillage reduction this fuel type actually gets."
        },
        "rt_displacementRate": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows"
          ],
          "description": "REFEC-3/4: the displaced-vapour rate blended between an uncontrolled and a fully controlled vehicle by the onboard-recovery penetration, and reduced by the Stage II program. Zero on a rate row whose pollutant-process is not Refueling Displacement Vapor Loss, because `rt_refuelingProcessID` is 0 there and matches no `rct_processID`."
        },
        "rt_displacementRowCount": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows"
          ],
          "description": "How many `refuelingcontroltechnology` rows the reg-class wildcard admits. It is 1 on every displacement rate row and 0 elsewhere -- the table carries regClassID 20 alone -- so the wildcard sum is a lookup here. A snapshot with two reg classes would make it 2 and the output row would be their sum, which is what the reference does."
        },
        "rt_spillageRateRaw": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows"
          ],
          "description": "REFEC-5/6 before the county-year existence gate."
        },
        "rt_spillageRate": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows"
          ],
          "description": "REFEC-5/6: (1 - Pspill) ((1 - T) refuelingSpillRate), 0.31 g/gallon on a pre-1996 model year and 0.155 from 1996. Zero on a rate row that is not Refueling Spillage Loss."
        },
        "rt_spillageRowCount": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows"
          ],
          "description": "Whether the spillage working table has a row for this rate row: a `sourcetypetechadjustment` match AND a synthesised county-year row for the fuel AND a `refuelingfactors` row for it. All three are INNER JOINs in REFEC-5."
        },
        "rt_refuelingRate": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The rate this refueling row applies to the chained energy. The two terms are DISJOINT -- a rate row's `rt_refuelingProcessID` is 18, or 19, or 0 -- so the sum is a union and not a double count, which `rt_refuelingRowCount` is the test of."
        },
        "rt_refuelingRowCount": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows"
          ],
          "description": "0 or 1 on every rate row, and 1 exactly where the refueling working tables have a row."
        },
        "rtDay_energyQuant": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows",
            "runspecday_rows"
          ],
          "description": "S17: BaseRateCalculator's MOVESWorkerOutput quantity, rate x activity. For an energy pollutant-process this is KILOJOULES and it is deliberately NOT divided by `rt_unitDivisor` -- the kJ-to-MillionBTU rebase happens in the output processor, AFTER every chained calculator has run (moves-framework engine.rs:1078-1086), so the refueling calculator sees kilojoules. Dividing here would make every refueling row 1,055,055.9 times too small."
        },
        "rtDay_chainedEnergy": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows",
            "runspecday_rows"
          ],
          "description": "REFEC-7's `MOVESWorkerOutput` scan: the Total Energy Consumption of this rate row's COHORT, summed over the run's energy pollutant-processes. It is a SELF-JOIN of the rate relation -- the refueling row and the energy rows it chains off are rows of one relation -- so the clause names its two sides with `syms`, exactly as brake wear's PM10 chain does (docs/esm-conventions.md 27.2).\n\nThe reference emits one refueling row per ENERGY row and lets the output group-by add them; summing first is the same number because neither refueling rate depends on the energy process. It is the same number here for a second reason as well, and that reason is measured: processes 2 and 90 contribute exactly 0, so the roadTypeID their rows would carry -- off-network, a different output key -- never arises. `run_offNetworkRoadTypeCount` and `pp_energyTotal` are the two halves of that."
        },
        "rtDay_quantRaw": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows",
            "runspecday_rows"
          ],
          "description": "REFEC-8: rate x energy / (energyContent x fuelDensity) -- grams of THC per gallon times gallons. The divisor guard is REFEC-7's inner join onto RefuelingFuelType and not a defensive zero check: electricity's divisor is 0, and 0.0 x energy / 0 would be a NaN that no key-set check would catch."
        },
        "rtDay_quant": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows",
            "runspecday_rows"
          ],
          "description": "S18's output-unit rebase. Both refueling processes carry Total Gaseous Hydrocarbons, a MASS pollutant, so the divisor is exactly 1 -- computed through `rspp_isEnergy` rather than assumed, and the three energy rate rows beside them carry 1,055,055.9, which is what makes the 1 a measurement."
        },
        "rt_refuelIsSelected": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows"
          ],
          "description": "Whether this rate row is a MOVESOutput row: its cohort survives the source-bin distribution's `stmyFraction > 0` rule, the refueling working table has a row for it, and REFEC-7's fuel-type join finds a divisor. Three inner joins, none of them a decision about the output -- 168 of the 1,148 candidates pass, 64 displacement and 104 spillage."
        },
        "rt_refuelPrefix": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows"
          ],
          "description": "An inclusive prefix count of the selection over the whole rate relation. One rank across BOTH refueling blocks rather than a per-block cohort ordinal, because the two blocks are different sizes -- 64 and 104 -- so there is no block length to decompose an output row number by (docs/esm-conventions.md 22)."
        },
        "rt_refuelRank": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The prefix count ZEROED on a non-member, so every emitted row has a dense 1..168 and every suppressed candidate has a 0 that no output ordinal can match."
        },
        "run_refuelRowCount": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "run_rows"
          ],
          "description": "168, computed from the chain, so `n_outputRefuelRow` is a CHECKED declaration and not a transcription."
        },
        "pp_refuelRowCount": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "runspecpollutantprocess_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The emitted row count per pollutant-process, before the day axis: 64 for 118, 104 for 119, and 0 for the other five. The two are DIFFERENT, which is the structural difference between this fixture and every earlier one -- `refuelingcontroltechnology` carries fuel types 1 and 5 only, so displacement loses the 40 diesel cohorts that spillage keeps."
        },
        "pp_energyTotal": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "runspecpollutantprocess_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The total chained energy each pollutant-process contributes, in kilojoules, summed over cohorts and day types. Non-zero for 9101 and EXACTLY ZERO for 9102 and 9190, and that pair of zeros is the whole of the road-type argument made measurable: start-exhaust rates are emitted on operating modes 101-108 and extended-idle rates on mode 200, `dc_W` is the drive-cycle distribution over the 23 RUNNING modes of the selected on-road road type, so the rate contraction has no partner for either. `run_offNetworkRoadTypeCount` = 0 is why that is the reference's answer too and not a coincidence of this document's shape."
        },
        "outRefuelOrdinal": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "output_rows"
          ],
          "description": "Which of the 168 emitted refueling rate rows this output row is, decomposed from the aggregate's own loop symbol. 168 x 2 day types = 336. There is no pollutant-process block coordinate here and there cannot be one: the displacement block is 64 rows and the spillage block 104, so a block-major decomposition would need a block LENGTH that does not exist. One rank over the whole rate relation is what replaces it, and the pollutant-process comes back through the rank join like every other key."
        },
        "out_refuelingRate": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "output_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The refueling rate the row carries, grams of THC per gallon delivered. Not a MOVESOutput column -- the comparator keys on the snapshot's own columns and ignores the rest -- but the one intermediate a disagreement is most quickly attributed to."
        },
        "out_chainedEnergy": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "output_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The Total Energy Consumption the row chains off, in kilojoules -- the same number for the displacement and the spillage row of one cohort, which is what makes their ratio the ratio of their two rates."
        },
        "run_selectedRoadTypeCount": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "run_rows"
          ],
          "description": "How many road types the RunSpec selects: 1. The positive control beside `run_offNetworkRoadTypeCount`'s zero -- without it a `runspecroadtype` that failed to load at all would look like `no off-network road type selected` (docs/esm-conventions.md 18.2)."
        },
        "run_hasCountyYearRow": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "run_rows"
          ],
          "description": "Whether `countyyear` carries a row for the run's county and year. It does, and both program adjustments on it are 0 -- so the two zeros below are a row that says zero and not a join that found nothing."
        }
      },
