        {
          "id": "the_cohort_row_set_is_the_same_125_for_every_pollutant_process",
          "description": "125 of the 164 candidates survive `stmyFraction > 0` and reach a `pollutantprocessmodelyear` row, and they are the same 125 for all SEVEN of the run's pollutant-processes -- which is what lets one cohort rank serve both refueling blocks and the energy spine. `run_cohortSelectionTotal` at 875 is that fact summed and would still be 875 if the seven selected different 125s, which is why the per-pollutant-process counts are asserted beside it.\n\n`pp_rateCohortCount` is the DIFFERENT question -- how many of those cohorts reach an `emissionrate` row -- and its answer is the more interesting one: 125 for 9101, 104 for 9102, and 0 for the other five. The 104 matters because it says the start-exhaust rate table genuinely matches this run's source bins; process 2 contributes nothing to the chained energy for a reason that has nothing to do with the rate lookup, and `the_energy_spine_is_running_exhaust_alone` is where that reason is measured.",
