        {
          "id": "the_drive_cycle_weights_are_a_distribution_over_the_twenty_three_running_modes",
          "description": "W, checked on the two properties that do not require the reference. It is a DISTRIBUTION: the weights sum to the avgSpeedFraction column's own total, which is 1 to that column's six stored significant figures and not exactly, so the gate is ABSOLUTE at 1e-5 and not relative (docs/esm-conventions.md 20.5). And it covers exactly 23 operating modes.\n\nTHE MODE COUNT IS WHAT SAYS THE ENERGY SPINE IS RUNNING EXHAUST ALONE. `emissionrate` carries 12,160 start-exhaust rates on operating modes 101-108 and 488 extended-idle rates on mode 200, and `opmodepolprocassoc` associates all of them with their pollutant-processes -- so the rate table is not what excludes them. This 23 is: `dc_W` is the drive-cycle classification's own distribution over the running modes of an on-network road type, it never produces a start or a hotelling mode, and the contraction of a 9102 rate against it has no partner. `pp_energyTotal` is the same fact as a number.",
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0.0,
            "end": 0.0
          },
          "tolerance": {
            "abs": 1e-05
          },
          "assertions": [
            {
              "variable": "dc_WTotal",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 1.0,
              "coords": {
                "runspecday_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "dc_WTotal",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 1.0,
              "coords": {
                "runspecday_rows": 2
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "dc_WModeCount",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 23.0,
              "coords": {
                "runspecday_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "dc_WModeCount",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 23.0,
              "coords": {
                "runspecday_rows": 2
              }
            }
          ]
        },
