        {
          "id": "the_worked_examples_reach_MOVESOutput_in_both_blocks",
          "description": "docs/process-refueling.md 6.1-6.4, asserted against the numbers MOVESOutput stores rather than against this document's own, at the six rows where each factor of the chain is the one that decides the answer. The displacement block's three span the control-technology blend end to end -- uncontrolled at MY 1980, a 0.348 blend at 1998, fully controlled at 2020 -- and its E85 rows check the second fuel's own vapour rate and divisor. The spillage block's three straddle the 1995/1996 penetration step on diesel, which is the fuel the displacement block does not have at all.\n\nThe key columns are asserted beside them because a rank join that found the wrong cohort would still produce a number: `out_SCC` is computed from four columns of the row itself, so 2201210418 against 2205210419 pins the fuel type, the process digit and the road type together. The tolerance is the reference's six-significant-figure column storage.",
