        {
          "id": "the_two_refueling_rates_are_disjoint_and_the_stage_ii_reductions_are_inert",
          "description": "REFEC-3/4 and REFEC-5/6 at the rate row, and the row count that turns them into the emitted key set.\n\nTHE TWO RATES ARE DISJOINT, and that is what lets one expression serve both blocks with no branch: each lookup joins `rt_refuelingProcessID` to its own table's `processID`, so a displacement rate row matches no `sourcetypetechadjustment` row and a spillage rate row matches no `refuelingcontroltechnology` row. `rt_refuelingRowCount` is 1 on both and 0 on the five pollutant-processes that are neither.\n\nTHE CONTROL-TECHNOLOGY BLEND IS LIVE. `refuelingTechAdjustment` is 0 through model year 1997, so a 1980 gasoline vehicle carries the uncontrolled 3.0152931 g/gallon; it is 1.0 at 2020, so a new one carries the controlled 0.0361 and nothing of the uncontrolled rate; and at 1998 it is 0.348, so the row carries 3.0152931 x 0.652 + 0.0361 x 0.348 = 1.9785339 -- a genuine convex blend, which is the assertion that separates this from a two-case lookup. Spillage's own penetration is a step: 0.31 g/gallon through 1995 and 0.155 from 1996.\n\nTHREE ZEROS, EACH FOR A DIFFERENT REASON, and they are the whole of why the two blocks are 64 and 104 cohorts rather than 125 each. Diesel has no `refuelingcontroltechnology` row at all, so its displacement rate and its row count are both 0. Electricity HAS a spillage row -- `sourcetypetechadjustment` is keyed by source type and model year and knows nothing about fuel -- and its rate is 0 because `refuelingfactors` gives electricity a `refuelingSpillRate` of 0; what actually drops those 21 cohorts is `rt_hasFuelDivisor`, REFEC-7's join onto RefuelingFuelType. A document that dropped them on the rate instead would agree on all 336 rows and be wrong the first time a fuel had a non-zero spill rate and no energy content.\n\nAND THE TWO STAGE II PROGRAM REDUCTIONS ARE ZERO, so both (1 - P) factors are exactly 1 and this fixture cannot see them at all (docs/esm-conventions.md 23): perturbing either moves no output cell. `run_hasCountyYearRow` is what says that is a row saying zero rather than a join finding nothing, and components/refueling_loss_rate.esm is where the two factors are checked at 0.2 and 0.3.",
